  "question": {
    "text": "Let in a series of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></math> observations, half of them&nbsp;are equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> and remaining half are equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></math>. Also by adding a constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> in each of these observations, the mean and standard deviation&nbsp;of new set become <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math>, respectively. Then&nbsp;the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is equal to :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>425</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>650</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>925</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let observations are denoted by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>x</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8721;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mover><mi>x</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>&#963;</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8721;</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mover><mi>x</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#963;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math></p><p>Now, adding a constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>y</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>x</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#963;</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#963;</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></math> (No change in S.D.)&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>425</mn></math></p>"
  }
